 ## Overview
-Grid-based LOD Simplification is a method for rendering large-scale voxel or blocky meshes at multiple levels of detail by quantizing vertex coordinates to a coarse grid and implicitly managing primitive visibility. It solves the problem of rendering distant geometry efficiently without storing multiple explicit mesh copies on the GPU, by sorting primitives into a "Progressively Ordered Primitive" (POP) buffer [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Mesh simplification via valence pattern removal](1931-mesh-simplification-via-valence-pattern-removal.md) which modifies topology, or [GPU-based Mesh Decimation via Edge Collapse](3505-gpu-based-mesh-decimation-via-edge-collapse.md) which requires complex graph operations, this method relies on simple coordinate rounding and sorting [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Linear Spline Simplification](3483-linear-spline-simplification.md) as it operates on discrete integer grids rather than continuous spline approximations [S2, unofficial].
+Grid-based LOD Simplification renders large-scale voxel or blocky meshes at multiple levels of detail by quantizing vertex coordinates to a coarse grid and implicitly managing primitive visibility [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering distant geometry efficiently without storing multiple explicit mesh copies on the GPU by sorting primitives into a Progressively Ordered Primitive (POP) buffer [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Mesh simplification via valence pattern removal](1931-mesh-simplification-via-valence-pattern-removal.md) which modifies topology, or [GPU-based Mesh Decimation via Edge Collapse](3505-gpu-based-mesh-decimation-via-edge-collapse.md) which requires complex graph operations, this method relies on simple coordinate rounding and sorting [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Linear Spline Simplification](3483-linear-spline-simplification.md) as it operates on discrete integer grids rather than continuous spline approximations [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
